  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed replacement windows, by reason of their proposed material and loss of original windows, fails to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the John-Innes Wilton Crescent Conservation Area, contrary to the NPPF 2024 sections 12 and 16, London Plan design policies D1, D4, and HC1, and Local Plan 2024 policies D12.1, D12.3, D12.4, and D12.5.",
    "Reason : 2 - INFORMATIVE\r\nNote to Applicant\r\nIn accordance with paragraph 38 of the NPPF, The London Borough of Merton  (LBM) takes a positive and proactive approach to development proposals focused on solutions. LBM works with applicants/agents in a positive and proactive manner by:\r\n\"\tOffering a pre-application advice and duty desk service. \r\n\"\tWhere possible, suggesting solutions to secure a successful outcome.\r\n\"\tAs appropriate, updating applicants/agents of any issues that may arise in the processing of their application.\r\nIn this instance:\r\n\"\tThe application was not considered to comply with the provisions of the Development Plan and NPPF as submitted, and would have required key material changes. The applicant/agent was informed of issues arising during consideration of the application and how these could potentially be overcome but sufficient information was not forthcoming. \r\n\"\tIt is noted that the applicant/agent did not engage in any pre-application discussions.\r\n\"\tThe applicant is advised to seek pre-application advice on any resubmission.\r\n"
  ],
